<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
	Vara is intentionally NOT sandboxed (no com.apple.security.app-sandbox).

	App Sandbox is fundamentally incompatible with Vara's core mechanics:
	  - global keyboard monitoring via a CGEventTap (system-wide hotkey),
	  - synthetic Cmd+V paste into the frontmost app of the user's choice,
	  - spawning the local Python Hviske speech runtime as a child process,
	  - connecting to arbitrary user-chosen LLM endpoints (Groq, OpenAI,
	    Ollama/DGX on the LAN, etc.).

	Enabling the sandbox would break these features and the product itself,
	so it is deliberately omitted. Note: because the app is not sandboxed,
	any "Helt privat / Completely private" UI copy must be softened to
	truthful wording (handled by the UI layer, not this entitlements file).

	HARDENED-RUNTIME RELAXATIONS (Release / notarization):
	The two com.apple.security.cs.* keys below exist SOLELY because Vara spawns
	a user-provided Python interpreter (the optional local Hviske Danish STT
	runtime) as a child process:
	  - disable-library-validation lets that python load unsigned third-party
	    native libraries (torch / numpy / soundfile dylibs) under the hardened
	    runtime, which would otherwise refuse to load code not signed by us or
	    Apple.
	  - allow-dyld-environment-variables lets the backend pass HF_HOME and
	    PYTORCH_ENABLE_MPS_FALLBACK into the spawned python's environment.
	Vara itself is pure Swift, so we deliberately do NOT add
	allow-unsigned-executable-memory or allow-jit.

	IMPORTANT: the Developer-ID re-sign step in scripts/build-dmg.sh MUST pass
	the codesign entitlements flag pointing at THIS file (codesign drops
	entitlements otherwise), so keep this committed copy in sync with
	project.yml. XcodeGen regenerates this file from project.yml; the committed
	copy must stay correct for that manual codesign invocation.
	(Note: XML comments may not contain a double-hyphen, so flag names are
	spelled out in prose here rather than with their leading dashes.)

	Only the microphone entitlement is strictly required at runtime; the two
	relaxations matter only for the notarized Release build.
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
